{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1134902-setting-and-meta-ideas","id":1134902,"title":"Setting and Meta Ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-28T12:33:33-07:00","id":1134902,"title":"Setting and Meta Ideas","content":"I am going to be running a Beast the Primordial game here at some point and as I read over the book I have here, I noticed that it had potential to fulfill a idea I had years ago and could never quite make work = Shapeshifters (or some such thing) ...<br /> <br /> So I am starting this thread to see if anyone wants to talk through this idea with me and offer their own suggestions about what I am doing and how they might expand on my ideas. <br /> <br /> With that said, here is the pitch =<br /> <br /> <b>Skinwalkers the Primordial </b><br /> <br /> The setting is currently set at 1865 to 1875 , in the USA, as a overarching theme for the Wild West. <br /> <br /> Skinwalkers are Spirits from the Hunting Grounds<br /> <br /> They can take the form of any animal they consume (in some way)<br /> <br /> This includes people...<br /> <br /> There is no Morality stat or Wisdom or Arete... there is instead a kind of &quot;Wendigo&quot; rating. <br /> <br /> Beasts are not on a path to enlightenment, nor are they evil. Like an animal, they simply exist. <br /> <br /> However, they are meant to exist in the Hunting Grounds , not here in this world<br /> <br /> The major conflict then is meant to be between Skinwalkers and Mankind. <br /> <br /> This conflict takes the form of what a Skinwalker needs to live here in this world, detached from the Hunting Grounds<br /> <br /> That this is essence of the Hunting Grounds, which are the Spirit Realm. <br /> <br /> This appears to be the same as any creature = they eat and they drink<br /> <br /> However, the only things that will nourish them are 'natural' things. Farmed grains, ranched animals, bottled water and such - any man-altered or man-farmed items offer no sustenance.<br /> <br /> This creates a dynamic that puts the Skinwalkers at odds against mankind's westward expansion. <br /> <br /> Yet as a kind of spirit beast, Skinwalkers are beasts, and as such they are unrepentant for their actions. This means that the player character are in some ways the 'antagonist' of the plot. <br /> <br /> And that the thing that takes the place of Frenzy or Backlash or Torment etc etc - is mankind .<br /> <br /> Or in more specific terms - Big Damn Heroes. <br /> <br /> The more you fight humanity the more you draw a kind of hero who is there to stop you, hunt you, kill you. <br /> <br /> Defeat them, and your legend grows, fail and you die.<br /> <br /> What happens when you die? Do you return to the Hunting Grounds you come from? <br /> - unknown at this time...<br /> <br /> Can you return to the Hunting Grounds while alive?<br /> - unknown at this time (but not as a matter of common course in the very least)<br /> <br /> What are you here? What brought you out of the Hunting Grounds?<br /> - Could be individual story teller plot<br /> - Could be major game setting event<br /> - Could be unknown<br /> - Could be strange facet of nature<br /> - other?<br /> <br /> <br /> SO<br /> With all that, if anyone wants to help me expand on the idea...<br /> <br /> Everything above is subject to needing more detail or maybe changes. <br /> - What more details does it need?<br /> - What changes does it need?<br /> <br /> And there are no real powers at this point (Disciplines, Rotes, Gifts, etc etc) <br /> - What powers should a Skinwalker have?<br /> <br /> How Should Skinwalkers be broken up?<br /> - Same as Beast the Primordial?<br /> - Animal family?<br /> <br /> How much should / can Native American lore fit into this? <br /> - Naive American lore...since they are natives and all<br /> - Chinese lore a little too from all the immigrants?<br /> - Other culture lore?<br /> <br /> Other ideas to fit into this ?<br /> <br /> Thanks!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15376-renleyrenfield","name":"RenleyRenfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15376_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T13:19:27-07:00","id":1134915,"title":"","content":"You know that CofD has Skinwalkers already, right? They got a 2e update in the first Dark Eras.<br /> <br /> Also, know that if you want to bring in actual Skinwalkers from Navajo myth, they're pretty well-documented as a real spiritual belief in a certain kind of witch. Tread very carefully if you want to go down that path, as it leads easily to stereotypes and appropriation.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Technically, the bunch in Dark Eras are called Skinchangers. They're in the Aztec chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 08-28-2017, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T13:38:00-07:00","id":1134925,"title":"","content":"Sounds like a ghost wolf lodge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-28-2017, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T13:59:43-07:00","id":1134938,"title":"","content":"Interesting. I'll be curious to see how this folds out. I'd suggest doing a hodge podge of lore, and using a little bit of what we know of werewolf, either from the Forsaken 2e book or from the Dark Eras books. Could be useful to your world building.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T14:08:01-07:00","id":1134943,"title":"","content":"What got me thinking in the first place was Beast = not Werewolf.<br /> <br /> The reason for that was the general idea behind what someone here said a long while back = that Beast has a different approach than all the rest. It is about being the Beast in a more complete way, more so than even werewolf which struggles with rage.<br /> <br /> The idea behind what I am twisting Beast into here, is more of a acceptance of the Beast as is (no moral code), and instead the focus becomes on survival and conflict with those NPCs that live by a moral code.<br /> <br /> The ideas from the Dark Eras book seems more setting and less of a deep mechanic I am looking for. (And I am not sure the Beast Mechanic is what i need, but it seems closest...)<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Honestly, I could run a game about sentient lollipops given enough time and inspiration :P<br /> <br /> So what I am looking for here, are not book references or a complete rule set.<br /> <br /> I just want to see if anyone is interested in running with the idea i have proposed and seeing where it leads.<br /> <br /> I have more ideas on it, but I wanted to see what others had to suggest or what inspired them first <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15376-renleyrenfield","name":"RenleyRenfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15376_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T14:57:34-07:00","id":1135272,"title":"","content":"Ah, fair enough. I was meaning specifically for information on the Spirit than anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}